{
  "requirement": "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is\ncheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors\nselect it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames\nwithout an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Each structural obligation is met.\n\n- **`OutlineLang` and `Default`:** The `language!(PlainText, super::plain::PROFILE)` invocation in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs` (`macro@8f870aac097a`) expands via `macro[language]`. It declares the unit struct `PlainText` and derives `Clone, Copy, Debug, Default`. The macro also implements `OutlineLang` with `name`, `extensions`, `outline`, `fingerprint_scheme` and `search_structure`, which matches `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`.\n- **Cheap cloning:** `PlainText` is a unit struct that derives `Copy`, so cloning shares nothing and copies nothing in proportion to size.\n- **No claimed extensions:** `extensions()` returns `$profile.extensions`. For `PlainText` that is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/plain.rs#static[PROFILE]`, which sets `extensions: &[]`.\n- **Selection when no language claims the extension:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#impl[OutlineContent]/fn[parse_source]` is the path used by `from_path` and `from_source`. It calls `languages::registry().for_path(filename)`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/language.rs#impl[Registry]/fn[for_path]` lowercases the extension, and it returns `None` for a missing extension (via `path.extension()?`) or an unclaimed one. `parse_source` then falls back to `Self::parse_with(&languages::PlainText, ...)`. This covers filenames without an extension, as `requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults` requires.\n\nThe `_with` constructors (`from_path_with`, `from_source_with`) take an explicit language and do no selection, so they don't affect this requirement.",
  "references": "614a1a6516d348267d0201851594c14314a25db22baa81a0d1100d7beb3ca048",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.language"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} language",
        "`languages::PlainText` implements `OutlineLang` under",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`. Its default value is",
        "cheaply cloneable and claims no extensions. The filename-based constructors",
        "select it when no supplied language claims the extension, including filenames",
        "without an extension, under {cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} language_provider",
        "",
        "`OutlineLang` defines the language interface. Each implementation supplies its",
        "name, claimed extensions, and outlining operation. Cloning a language shares",
        "its prepared configuration instead of rebuilding it or copying it in proportion",
        "to its size. Its result uses the public items, spans, and hashes under",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.items`. Filename extensions omit the leading dot.",
        "",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "pub trait OutlineLang:",
        "    Clone",
        "    + Send",
        "    + Sync {",
        "    fn name(&self) -> &str;",
        "    fn extensions(&self) -> &[&str];",
        "    fn outline(&self, source: &str) -> Result<Outline, OutlineError>;",
        "    fn fingerprint_scheme(&self) -> &str;",
        "",
        "    fn search_structure(",
        "        &self,",
        "        _source: &str,",
        "        _rule: &Map<String, Value>,",
        "    ) -> Result<Vec<Span>, OutlineError> { ... }",
        "}",
        "```",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.outlines.defaults"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} defaults",
        "The filename-based constructors include Rust, Python, TypeScript, TSX,",
        "Markdown, CSS, TOML, and YAML languages. Extension matching is",
        "case-insensitive, using each implementation's claimed extensions.",
        "The [language chapters](#language-specific-rules) define those mappings.",
        "A filename without a claimed extension uses the",
        "[plain-text outline](sources/plain-text.md): a file root with one child per",
        "nonblank line.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
